The usual question the information you provide needs
to convey, is, what have _you changed_ between the
problem not occurring and the problem occurring.

Since Microsoft tries very hard to _impose_ upgrades
on your system, a second question might be what has
Microsoft/Vista changed between the problem not
occurring and the problem occurring.

It's also of interest over how long a period between
"it works" and "it doesn't work" you played no
NetHack; that's the period within which a search for
the problem's entry point must happen.

Microsoft has put out at least one security update
that, at least on my WinXP system, broke _lots_ of
third party software, and I seem to remember that
update being common to WinXP and WinVista.

All that ignored for the moment, possible sources of
your problem might be:

You reinstalled NetHack and something went wrong;
perhaps you installed a WinXP version when a
WinVista version was appropriate.

You downgraded your operating system from WinXP to
WinVista and some needed font support went missing.

A WinVista patch from Microsoft broke something.

You uninstalled the font NetHack was using, or installed
one or more new fonts that somehow overwrote that font or
intercepted access to it, or modified the search path for
the font.

